    "Give shoulders a little more attention: try adding one set to your shoulder training to gradually bring that volume share up and support long-term joint health and upper body balance.",
    "Continue your current approach to chest and back: both groups are progressing strongly with 6 sets each, so maintain that structure and keep adding load or reps wherever you can to sustain the overload."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "All six muscle groups posted strong strength index gains (4 to 7 points each) in a full week of 28 sets; legs led progress and minor volume gaps exist in biceps and shoulders."
